<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gagik II of Armenia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1025–1079</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gagik II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> was the last king of the Bagratid dynasty of Ani, crowned in 1042 as a young man. Summoned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, he was pressured into surrendering his capital and kingdom to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in 1045, in line with the bequest of his uncle Hovhannes-Smbat. He was given estates in Cappadocia and was killed there around 1079.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gagik-ii-of-armenia.jpg" alt="Gagik II of Armenia" width="320" height="135" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, 13th-century author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakikios_surrenders_to_Constantine_IX.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
